ub.com/users/Foyezes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Foyezes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T06:48:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T06:48:06Z","body":"HDRI without fog:\n<img width=\"1638\" height=\"987\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1cc5f893-6b5b-45e2-a9a4-40032570730f\" />\n\nHDRI with fog enabled:\n<img width=\"1638\" height=\"987\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5374a785-fd3f-4613-85f3-4005372ea6b1\" />\n\nThe sky doesn't affect the cube once fog is enabled, which wasn't the case in earlier versions such as 4.7. I normally use fog to set a flat background while keeping the HDRI lighting, but now it seems like it affects lighting too - which is fine if it's the intended result.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6309901954/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6353927104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124350#issuecomment-6353927104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124350","id":6353927104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABerk7wA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-22T23:53:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T23:53:05Z","body":">  I normally use fog to set a flat background while keeping the HDRI lighting, but now it seems like it affects lighting too - which is fine if it's the intended result.\n\nThis is intended as per https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107958. If you want separate background and sky colors (e.g. for green screen effects), set the **Background > Mode** option to **Custom Color** and keep the sky option as it is.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6353927104/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]